## Reviewer points not applied
- a#8 Hangul urls. ACCEPTED-ROUND says the frontmatter url is not edited.
- a#23 „znatan iznos“. That puts the received-amount result back into the anecdote R3 tells the fixer to keep as an entitlement. The tautology was removed; the result claim was not restored.
- a#25 and the space-separator half of a#26 and b#37, including „1,57 milijuna TWD“ and „500 000“. The checker parses hr amounts only with a dot. TWD 1.57M stays byte-identical.
- a#29 inflected „jedne / jednog / jednu“. Those forms are not in the number lexicon, so replacing the digit would fail the number check. The spurious „once“ was removed; the real counts stay as digits.
- a#33 and any deletion of U+200B. Promoting Q16–Q20 to headings, or deleting the zero-width spaces, fails the block check. The visible sign-off was rephrased; the invisible characters stayed.
- b#8 without the digit 1. The negligence multiple stays „1 puta“.
- b#21 as one merged paragraph. Merging changes the block count. Each 013 and 015 fragment was completed in its own paragraph.
- a#22’s English „Easy“. Calling economic dismissal easy is the outcome tone R3 softens. The row now says the difficulty cannot be called easy in advance.
